[{"q":"When cycling, wear a ____.","options":["blindfold","long loose scarf in the wheel","helmet","earphones at full volume always"],"answer":2,"explain":"Helmets protect the head."},{"q":"Your body is private. If someone touches you in a bad way, ____.","options":["hide at the market","tell a trusted adult","blame yourself","keep silent forever"],"answer":1,"explain":"It is not your fault. Speak up."},{"q":"When the alarm rings, ____.","options":["ignore it","follow emergency instructions","lock yourself in the toilet always","run in any direction screaming only"],"answer":1,"explain":"Practise drills seriously."},{"q":"Do not fight. Fighting can cause ____.","options":["peace always","more friends always","better exam scores","injury"],"answer":3,"explain":"Use words or a teacher, not fists."},{"q":"In a fire, ____ to the nearest exit.","options":["go back for toys first always","move quickly and calmly","hide under a nylon bag","use the lift in a burning house if told never"],"answer":1,"explain":"Know the escape route. Don’t use lifts in a fire."},{"q":"Nigeria’s national emergency number is ____.","options":["1234","911 only as the only option","112","000"],"answer":2,"explain":"112 is the national emergency number."},{"q":"If you get lost in a market, ____.","options":["stay put and look for a security post / tell a seller with a stall to find police","follow any stranger home","hide in a boot of a car","leave town"],"answer":0,"explain":"Stay visible and ask official help."},{"q":"The police emergency number often taught is ____.","options":["12","0000","7777","199"],"answer":3,"explain":"199 can reach the police."},{"q":"In a stampede, move ____ the crowd if you can, protect your chest.","options":["by sitting in the middle","deeper into","sideways out of","against blindly"],"answer":2,"explain":"Protect yourself; don’t push."},{"q":"If a stranger asks you to go with them, you should ____.","options":["keep it secret","enter the car","follow quietly","say no and tell an adult"],"answer":3,"explain":"Never go with a stranger."},{"q":"Do not play with ____.","options":["story books","puzzles","fire and matches","a football in a field"],"answer":2,"explain":"Fire can burn."},{"q":"A whistle can be used to ____ for help.","options":["cook","call","sweep","iron"],"answer":1,"explain":"Loud signals attract attention."},{"q":"Do not walk alone in ____ places.","options":["a busy school corridor","dark lonely","a supervised playground","your living room"],"answer":1,"explain":"Stay where people can see you."},{"q":"Online, do not share your ____.","options":["class","favourite subject","first name only with teacher","address and password"],"answer":3,"explain":"Personal data can be misused."},{"q":"Do not take ____ given by friends without an adult’s knowledge.","options":["unknown drugs or tablets","your own lunch","a textbook","your own water bottle"],"answer":0,"explain":"Unknown substances can harm you."},{"q":"Do not take gifts from ____.","options":["grandparents","strangers","your teacher as a prize","your parents"],"answer":1,"explain":"Strangers may not be safe."},{"q":"Security education teaches us to stay ____.","options":["safe","away from school","afraid of everyone forever","silent in class always"],"answer":0,"explain":"Be alert, not fearful."},{"q":"Report suspicious bags in public to ____.","options":["nobody","your younger sibling only","a stranger to open it","security / police"],"answer":3,"explain":"Do not touch unknown packages."},{"q":"The assembly point is where we ____ in an emergency.","options":["play football first","hide from teachers","buy snacks","meet"],"answer":3,"explain":"Schools have assembly points."},{"q":"A good security habit at home is to ____ the door.","options":["hide the key under the mat always","tell strangers where the key is","leave wide open at night always","lock"],"answer":3,"explain":"Lock doors and windows."},{"q":"When crossing the road, look ____, right and left again.",